  "summary": "Apple’s revenue appears as 13 separate XBRL rows for FY 2022 because the company files distinct financial statements for each quarter (10‑Q) and an annual report (10‑K). Each filing contains the same revenue concept (RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax), resulting in multiple instances that add up to 13 rows across the four filings.",
  "claims": [
    "In the Q2 2022 10‑Q filing (accession 0000320193-22-000059), Apple reported 4 instances of the RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax concept.",
    "In the Q3 2022 10‑Q filing (accession 0000320193-22-000070), Apple reported 4 instances of the RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax concept.",
    "In the FY 2022 10‑K filing (accession 0000320193-22-000108), Apple reported 3 instances of the RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax concept.",
    "In the Q1 2022 10‑Q filing (accession 0000320193-22-000007), Apple reported 2 instances of the RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax concept."
  ]
}
